{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600202",
      "title": "Connecting Redux Toolkit State",
      "sourceHash": "044c17ca5665a8c366e541078368067918856137c5af4b4091dd253a24f99c3f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.87,
          "en": "Now to use our slice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.87,
          "end": 7.16,
          "en": "we first of all need to use the return value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.16,
          "end": 11,
          "en": "of calling createSlice because here we get back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11,
          "end": 14.79,
          "en": "our counterSlice, now this name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.79,
          "end": 17.54,
          "en": "but it's a slice of our global state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.54,
          "end": 19.55,
          "en": "the slice which is responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.55,
          "end": 21.633,
          "en": "for working with our counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.2,
          "end": 28.2,
          "en": "Now we wanna register this with our store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.75,
          "end": 30.34,
          "en": "So first of all we can get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.34,
          "end": 34.24,
          "en": "of our old counterReducer here, we don't need that anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.24,
          "end": 36.95,
          "en": "So let's remove it to make this a bit more readable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.95,
          "end": 39.37,
          "en": "And now here to createStore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.37,
          "end": 44.18,
          "en": "we could pass our counterSlice.reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.18,
          "end": 49.18,
          "en": "With that we get access to the reducers set up in the slice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.47,
          "end": 53.74,
          "en": "even though it .reducer, it's basically a big reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.74,
          "end": 55.42,
          "en": "with a couple of if statements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.42,
          "end": 58,
          "en": "that trigger those different reducer methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58,
          "end": 62.228,
          "en": "depending on the action type and we would be good to go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.228,
          "end": 64.67,
          "en": "Now we just couldn't dispatch actions right now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.67,
          "end": 68.78,
          "en": "but in theory, we would be good to go like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.78,
          "end": 71.17,
          "en": "But if we have bigger applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.17,
          "end": 73.48,
          "en": "with multiple state slices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.48,
          "end": 76.9,
          "en": "we would face a problem if we try to do it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.9,
          "end": 79.25,
          "en": "because there can only be one reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.25,
          "end": 82.94,
          "en": "passed to create store and when we have multiple slices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.94,
          "end": 87.56,
          "en": "we have multiple reducers which we access with .reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.56,
          "end": 88.863,
          "en": "on the different slices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.35,
          "end": 94.16,
          "en": "Now with standard Redux, there is a combineReducers function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.59,
          "end": 99.88,
          "en": "which we could use for that but we can also ditch Redux here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.88,
          "end": 104.1,
          "en": "and instead import another function from reduxjs/toolkit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.1,
          "end": 106.41,
          "en": "which will make that a bit easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.41,
          "end": 109.13300000000001,
          "en": "We can import the configureStore function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.265,
          "end": 114.64,
          "en": "ConfigureStore like createStore creates a store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.64,
          "end": 117.28999999999999,
          "en": "but it makes merging multiple reducers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.28999999999999,
          "end": 121,
          "en": "into one reducer easier thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121,
          "end": 124.54,
          "en": "So here we can now call configureStore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.54,
          "end": 128.45,
          "en": "and to configureStore, we now pass an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 128.45,
          "end": 131.58,
          "en": "not a reducer function but an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.58,
          "end": 135.963,
          "en": "It's a configuration object expected by configureStore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 136.99,
          "end": 141.99,
          "en": "A configuration object where we then set a reducer property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 143.77,
          "end": 146.863,
          "en": "and that's an expected property by configureStore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 147.76,
          "end": 152.49,
          "en": "Reducer singular and not reducers plural",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 152.49,
          "end": 156.475,
          "en": "because still, no matter if we use createStore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 156.475,
          "end": 161.475,
          "en": "or configureStore, Redux wants one main reducer function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 161.92000000000002,
          "end": 165.32999999999998,
          "en": "which is responsible for the global state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 165.32999999999998,
          "end": 168.36,
          "en": "However, with configureStore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 168.36,
          "end": 173.36,
          "en": "the value for reducer can be a single reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 174.05,
          "end": 178.94,
          "en": "so we can for example use counterSlice.reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 178.94,
          "end": 181.19,
          "en": "to use the reducer from that counterSlice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 182.04,
          "end": 184.56,
          "en": "which combines all those reducer methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 184.56,
          "end": 186.61,
          "en": "to find in that slice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 186.61,
          "end": 191.08,
          "en": "We can use that as a global main reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 191.08,
          "end": 192.92,
          "en": "and here that would make sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 192.92,
          "end": 195.76,
          "en": "because this is the only state slice we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 195.76,
          "end": 198.453,
          "en": "and therefore, the only reducer we have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 199.44,
          "end": 204.44,
          "en": "but if we had multiple state slices in a bigger application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 204.65,
          "end": 206.82999999999998,
          "en": "something we're going to see later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 206.82999999999998,
          "end": 211.82999999999998,
          "en": "then alternatively as a value for this reducer key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 211.85,
          "end": 216.85,
          "en": "we could also set an object and in that object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 217,
          "end": 220.11,
          "en": "we can set up any keys of our choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 220.11,
          "end": 222.74,
          "en": "so any property names of our choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 222.74,
          "end": 225.16,
          "en": "and the values of those properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 225.16,
          "end": 228.7,
          "en": "would then be different reducer functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 228.7,
          "end": 233.18,
          "en": "So we would create a map of reducers you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 233.18,
          "end": 238.18,
          "en": "and this map is then set as a value for the main reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 238.3,
          "end": 240.52,
          "en": "and behind the scenes configureStore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 241.39,
          "end": 246.18,
          "en": "will emerge all those reducers into one big reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 246.18,
          "end": 248.95,
          "en": "So it will merge them for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 248.95,
          "end": 252.22,
          "en": "And that's an alternative we can use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 252.22,
          "end": 255.49,
          "en": "not an alternative we will use here though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 255.49,
          "end": 258.42,
          "en": "because here we only have one reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 258.42,
          "end": 260.38,
          "en": "so we can direct the assign,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 260.38,
          "end": 263.287,
          "en": "that reducer from the counterSlice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 263.287,
          "end": 267.423,
          "en": "as our main reducer for configureStore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 268.54,
          "end": 272.76,
          "en": "Now the question is, how do we dispatch actions?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 272.76,
          "end": 275.84000000000003,
          "en": "Because we don't have our own, if checks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 275.84000000000003,
          "end": 278.85,
          "en": "we don't know what the identifiers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 278.85,
          "end": 280.84000000000003,
          "en": "for our actions should be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 280.84000000000003,
          "end": 282.74,
          "en": "We just have these method names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 282.74,
          "end": 285.313,
          "en": "but how do we now know what to dispatch?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}